{"name":"Hoarfrost","hex":"#dbecfb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hoarfrost","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of hoar frost."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hoarfrost"}],"entries":[{"title":"Frost","blocks":[{"text":"Frost is a layer of ice on a solid surface, which forms from water vapor that deposits onto a freezing surface. Frost forms when the air contains more water vapor than it can normally hold at a specific temperature. The process is similar to the formation of dew, except it occurs below the freezing point of water typically without crossing through a liquid state."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg/330px-Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frost","wikidata":"Q4590598"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Nevada-Apartadero-Merida-Venezuela.jpg/500px-Nevada-Apartadero-Merida-Venezuela.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Nevada-Apartadero-Merida-Venezuela.jpg/1280px-Nevada-Apartadero-Merida-Venezuela.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Nevada-Apartadero-Merida-Venezuela.jpg/500px-Nevada-Apartadero-Merida-Venezuela.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Frost in the highest town in Venezuela, Apartaderos: Because of its location in an alpine tundra ecosystem called páramo, a daily freeze-and-thaw cycle, sometimes described as \"summer every day and winter every night\", exists.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANevada-Apartadero-Merida-Venezuela.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c